    "summary": "Cloth (Yoruba aso oke) composed of 14 strips hand-woven from imported industrial cotton, and hand-sewn together along the selvedges. The strips are all identical, and the pattern is entirely in the warp, the weft being entirely of black yarn. This pattern is formed from a narrow line of yellow along the centre; on one side of this is a broad band of maroon edged by a much narrower band of green; on the other side are alternating thin lines of light blue, mid blue, and black thread. The ends have been hemmed.",
